# Downloaded encoders and scratch artefacts are not ours to version. The TRAINED SCORER is: it is 27 KB,
# it is this project's actual output, and without it in the repo the LLM-free judge cannot run for anyone
# but the machine that trained it — which is exactly how a shipped Action would have had no model at all.
# The training report ships with it as provenance: which corpus, which encoder hash, which thresholds.
# Note the shape: `models/*` and not `models/`. Git does not descend into an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so a
# negation under `models/` can never fire and the files could only be added with `git add -f` — which
# means a future retrain would silently not be committed. Each level has to be re-included in turn.
# The weights now live in `@a11y-witness/scorer` (PLAN.md M3), so only the ENCODER is ignored — the 27 KB of
# heads and the training report are tracked, and nothing under `packages/scorer/models` needs re-including
# level by level because no ancestor is excluded any more. The lesson above still applies to `models/*`
# below, which is kept because a retrain writes its intermediate output there.
packages/scorer/models/encoders/

# `npm pack` includes UNTRACKED files, so the encoder sitting inside the package directory would be shipped
# to every consumer if `packages/scorer/package.json` listed `models` instead of `models/screenreader-scorer`.
# That is why the allow-list names the subdirectory.

models/*

# Corpus snapshots (scripts/corpus-snapshot.mjs) — local archives, never committed
backups/

# tsc --build output from the project-reference fixtures (src/packaging/project-references.test.ts)
scripts/tsconfig-fixtures/*/dist/
scripts/tsconfig-fixtures/*/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Package build output (npm run build)
packages/*/dist/
packages/*/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
